workedExamples.question_text:
This plan of a garden uses a scale of $1:250$. Its labelled length on the plan is $8$ cm. Find the real length in metres.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (4,2);
\path (2,1) node {Garden} (2,0) node[below=3mm] {$8\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

On this plan, the $3$ cm wall represents $12$ m in real life. Find the real length of the wall labelled $5$ cm.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (4,2.4);
\path (2,0) node[below=3mm] {$5\text{ cm}$} (0,1.2) node[left=3mm] {$3\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
This scale drawing of a garden uses a scale of $1:200$.
Find the real length of the garden, in metres.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (4,2.4);
\node[below] at (2,0) {$6\text{ cm}$};
\node at (2,1.2) {Garden};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.question_text:
This scale drawing of a swimming pool uses a scale of $1:400$.
Find the real length and real width of the pool, in metres.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (4,2.4);
\node[below] at (2,0) {$5\text{ cm}$};
\node[left] at (0,1.2) {$3\text{ cm}$};
\node at (2,1.2) {Pool};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

mastery.question_text:
